.TH SIMPLEZIP 1 "2026" "SimpleZip" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simplezip \- SimpleZip command-line companion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simplezip
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simplezip
drives the same archive engines as the SimpleZip app from your terminal, with
real exit codes for scripts and CI. It is installed as a symlink at
.I /usr/local/bin/simplezip
from SimpleZip \(-> Settings \(-> General \(-> Command-Line Tool.
.PP
Every finished command is also recorded in the app's Activity Center.
Passwords are never accepted as command-line arguments.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B open \fIfile\fR...
Open files or archives in the SimpleZip app (equivalent to double-clicking).
.TP
.B check \fIarchive\fR...
Test archive integrity with the bundled 7\-Zip engine. Exits 1 if any archive
fails; a summary line is printed for the run.
.TP
.B compare \fIleft\fR \fIright\fR
Compare the entry lists of two archives (path, size, CRC, modified, encryption).
Exits 1 when they differ.
.TP
.B create \fIoutput\fR \fIinput\fR... [\fIoptions\fR]
Create an archive; the format comes from the output extension (zip, 7z, tar,
tar.gz, ...). Your saved per-format defaults apply. Never overwrites an existing
file.
.TP
.B verify \fIchecksum-file\fR...
Verify the files listed in a checksum file (sha256sum / BSD tag / bare digest /
\&.sfv). Unsafe entries (absolute paths, ..) are rejected. Exits 1 on any failure.
.TP
.B list \fIarchive\fR
List an archive's entries (kind, size, name). Read-only.
.TP
.B inspect \fIarchive\fR
Release-package check without extracting (counts, junk, empty dirs, executables,
symlinks, suspicious paths). Exits 1 when suspicious paths are found.
.TP
.B extract \fIarchive\fR... [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIdir\fR]
Extract each archive into a uniquely named folder via the same vetted safe path as
Finder auto-extract. \fB\-\-to\fR sets the destination parent. Exits 1 on any failure.
.TP
.B hash \fIfile\fR... [\fB\-\-algo\fR \fIlist\fR]
Compute checksums (CRC32, MD5, SHA1, SHA256, SHA512; default SHA256; or
.B all\fR).
BSD-tag output that \fBverify\fR can read back.
.TP
.B space \fIarchive\fR
Disk-usage breakdown (original vs packed, ratio, junk, largest files/folders/extensions).
.TP
.B rescue \fIarchive\fR [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIdir\fR]
Best-effort recovery from a damaged archive into a "(rescued)" folder. The archive is
not repaired. Exits 1 if nothing could be recovered.
.TP
.B checkup \fIarchive\fR...
Batch integrity test plus suspicious/junk/encrypted counts over several archives (or a
folder). Exits 1 if any archive fails its integrity test.
.TP
.B duplicates \fIpath\fR...
Find duplicate archives by structural fingerprint among the given archives (or a folder).
.TP
.B reproduce \fIfolder\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR \fIzip\fR|\fI7z\fR]
Pack a folder twice and report whether the two builds are byte-for-byte identical.
Exits 1 when they differ.
.TP
.B audit \fIfolder\fR
Audit a release directory (SHA256SUMS coverage, stale entries, broken VERIFY references,
orphans). Exits 1 when an artifact is uncovered.
.TP
.B verify-group \fIfolder\fR
Fast, name-only release-group check (is it verifiable?). Exits 1 when it isn't.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the CLI environment: the app bundle, the bundled 7\-Zip engine, the optional
RAR and GPG backends, and the symlink.
.TP
.B completions \fIzsh\fR|\fIbash\fR|\fIfish\fR
Print a shell completion script to stdout.
.TP
.B version
Print the app version this CLI belongs to.
.TP
.B help \fR[\fIcommand\fR]
Show help, or detailed help for one command.
.SH "CREATE OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-template, \-t \fIname\fR
Apply a saved task template by stable slug.
.TP
.B \-\-level, \-l \fI0\-9\fR
Compression level.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-junk
Skip .DS_Store, AppleDouble, Thumbs.db and desktop.ini.
.TP
.B \-\-reproducible
Deterministic output (zip/7z): same input, byte\-identical archive.
.TP
.B \-\-encrypt
Encrypt the archive. The password is read from the
.B SIMPLEZIP_PASSWORD
environment variable, or prompted interactively (never echoed). It is never
accepted as a command\-line argument.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON result object per command on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet, \-q
Only errors and the exit code.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Stream the backend's raw output.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failures or differences found.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or environment error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SIMPLEZIP_PASSWORD
Password used by \fBcreate \-\-encrypt\fR when set (otherwise prompted on the tty).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
SimpleZip.app, 7zz(1)
